    "media:imagetext": "I think that present-day food,\npresent-day eating habits are\ngetting too staid... Why can't\nwe eat adventurous food?...\nI have often wondered why a\nman will enter a roomful of\nstrangers or move into a new\ncommunity, but he will not\nsample a strange dish. What\nmakes us so bold in our\nhuman relationships, yet so\nfearful of adventurous eat-\ning? Both can be very re-\nwarding experiences,\nyou\nknow. So I say to the chefs of\nthe world: create! And I say\nto the diners of the world:\nenjoy!\nSendie\nAlohe/\nWHISKIES\nBOURBON\nSCOTCH\nCANADIAN\nTENNESSEE\nCOCKTAILS\nMENEHUNE JUICE\nMAI TAI\nUNITED'S VERY DRY MARTINI\n(GIN OR VODKA)\nOLD FASHIONED\nMANHATTAN\nDAIQUIRI\nBLOODY MARY\nSPANISH SHERRY\nGIN VODKA\nRUM\nWINES\nCHAMPAGNE (Split)\nCOLD DUCK (Split)\n•RED WINE (Split)\nLIQUEURS:\nBENEDICTINE AND BRANDY\nCOGNAC\nDRAMBUIE\nONE DOLLAR EACH\n***\nBEER — FIFTY CENTS EACH\n***\nSALTED NUTS\nMinors Will Not Be Served Liquor.\nHawaiian flight liquor is tax exempt.\nPapaaina\n(Menu)\nCLAM COCKTAIL DIP\nClams in seasoned cream cheese make this an outstanding dip.\nLIME ASPIC WITH CRAB, BENGAL DRESSING\nCurry flavored dressing tops this aspic.\nTRADER VIC'S OLD FASHIONED WINE CUP\nBROILED BEEF TENDERLOIN, MALAGASY\nTender steak made with sweet peppercorn butter.\nALMOND POTATO\nMashed potatoes with roasted almonds.\nBROCCOLI PUFF\nA broccoli souffle with a touch of nutmeg.\nor\nINDONESIAN PORK ROAST WITH PEANUT SAUCE\nA small rib roast of pork marinated in honey and lemon,\ntopped with a delicious peanut sauce.\nPEACH WITH CHUTNEY\nJust what it says, and delicious.\nCORN PUFF\nA corn souffle.\nCRISP DINNER ROLL\nMACADAMIA NUT MOUSSE CHANTILLY\nA light, refreshing Macadamia nut cream pudding.\nCOFFEE\nTEA\nMILK\nMENEHUNE TROPICAL MINT\nSFO",
